# How to fence node "node-a" via Redfish (fence_redfish).
# The file name MUST match the DRBD node name. Mode 0600 -- holds credentials.
#
# 'ip'/'ipport' point at node-a's Redfish BMC. Drop 'ssl_insecure=1' and use a
# trusted certificate in production. 'systems_uri' is the ComputerSystem for
# this host (often /redfish/v1/Systems/1 or /redfish/v1/Systems/System.Embedded.1
# on real hardware).
#
# SELinux note: the handler runs as drbd_t, which is allowed to connect to HTTP
# ports (see README). A BMC on a NON-standard port needs:
#     semanage port -a -t http_port_t -p tcp <port>
AGENT=/usr/sbin/fence_redfish
ip=10.0.0.1
ipport=443
ssl_insecure=1
username=admin
password=CHANGEME
systems_uri=/redfish/v1/Systems/1
# No 'delay=' here: the handler computes the priority-fencing-delay itself
# (Primary-majority node fences first). See FENCE_DELAY in fence.conf.
